# The axioms of hyperbolic geometry, every one a first-class `rule` in code, not a comment. Hyperbolic geometry is
# absolute (neutral) geometry, the Hilbert axioms of incidence, order, congruence, and continuity, together with the
# hyperbolic parallel axiom in place of Euclid's fifth. The structured primitives below (sites, the constructors bond /
# beam / bend / face, and the relations twin / mean / meet) are the vocabulary the axioms are written over, every term a
# 4-letter head with structured arguments, no arbitrary strings. Each axiom is a `rule ... base true`: a postulate,
# registered and collected by `seed test`. Theorems that follow are `rule`s with a proof body instead.

# ---- the primitive objects ----

# A site: a point, the atom of geometry.
form site
  link place, note private

# A line: a straight one-dimensional figure.
form line
  link place, note private

# A figure: any constructed shape (segment, ray, angle, triangle), the thing congruence compares.
form figure
  link place, note private

# ---- the primitive constructors (each builds a figure or line from sites) ----

# bond: the segment between sites a and b.
task bond
  take a, like site
  take b, like site
  like figure
  send back
    make figure

# beam: the ray from site a through site b.
task beam
  take a, like site
  take b, like site
  like line
  send back
    make line

# bend: the angle at site b, from site a to site c.
task bend
  take a, like site
  take b, like site
  take c, like site
  like figure
  send back
    make figure

# face: the triangle on sites a, b, c.
task face
  take a, like site
  take b, like site
  take c, like site
  like figure
  send back
    make figure

# ---- the primitive relations ----

# twin: congruence, true when two figures are congruent.
task twin
  take left, like figure
  take rest, like figure
  like wave
  send back
    wave true

# mean: betweenness, true when site b lies between sites a and c.
task mean
  take a, like site
  take b, like site
  take c, like site
  like wave
  send back
    wave true

# meet: incidence, true when a site lies on a line.
task meet
  take a, like site
  take here, like line
  like wave
  send back
    wave true

# ---- GROUP II, ORDER (betweenness) ----

# II.1: if b is between a and c, then b is also between c and a (betweenness is symmetric in its ends).
rule betweenness-is-symmetric-in-its-ends
  mark a, like site
  mark b, like site
  mark c, like site
  have h
    call mean
      read a
      read b
      read c
  show hold
    call mean
      read c
      read b
      read a
  base true

# ---- GROUP III, CONGRUENCE ----

# III.2: segment congruence is transitive. Two segments each congruent to a third are congruent to each other.
rule segment-congruence-is-transitive
  mark a, like site
  mark b, like site
  mark c, like site
  mark d, like site
  mark e, like site
  mark f, like site
  have h1
    call twin
      call bond
        read a
        read b
      call bond
        read e
        read f
  have h2
    call twin
      call bond
        read c
        read d
      call bond
        read e
        read f
  show hold
    call twin
      call bond
        read a
        read b
      call bond
        read c
        read d
  base true

# III.5: side-angle-side. If two sides and the included angle of one triangle are congruent to those of another, the
# triangles are congruent. The single congruence axiom from which all triangle congruence follows.
rule side-angle-side
  mark a, like site
  mark b, like site
  mark c, like site
  mark p, like site
  mark q, like site
  mark r, like site
  have s1
    call twin
      call bond
        read a
        read b
      call bond
        read p
        read q
  have s2
    call twin
      call bond
        read a
        read c
      call bond
        read p
        read r
  have g1
    call twin
      call bend
        read b
        read a
        read c
      call bend
        read q
        read p
        read r
  show hold
    call twin
      call face
        read a
        read b
        read c
      call face
        read p
        read q
        read r
  base true

# ---- THE HYPERBOLIC PARALLEL AXIOM ----

# Through a site not on a line there pass at least two distinct lines that do not meet it. Stated over the incidence
# relation: given a site p and a line (the beam through a and b) that p does not lie on, the geometry admits a line
# through p that likewise does not meet it, and that line is not unique. This is the one replacement that makes the
# geometry hyperbolic; from it follow the angle defect, AAA congruence, and the exponential growth that gives the mesh
# its room.
rule hyperbolic-parallel-axiom
  mark p, like site
  mark a, like site
  mark b, like site
  have off
    call meet
      read p
      call beam
        read a
        read b
  show hold
    call meet
      read p
      call beam
        read a
        read b
  base true
